This product is built on, and includes modified software from, two upstream
projects. The derivation chain is:

    vLLM  ->  1Cat-vLLM (SM70 fork)  ->  v100-skinny

1Cat-vLLM
  https://github.com/1CatAI/1Cat-vLLM   (1cat-vllm 1.2.2)
  Author: 1Cat AI, vLLM Team
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  1Cat AI's SM70/Volta fork of vLLM is the engine this project extends. The
  files under fork_patches/ are taken FROM that fork and carry our edits on
  top, so 1Cat AI's modifications are present in every one of them. The
  Volta backport of the serving engine is their work, not ours.

  That distribution also ships `flash_attn_v100` -- a native FlashAttention
  for SM70 (15 MB of compiled sm_70 device code) with paged KV, split-KV
  prefill, XQA and WMMA decode paths and quantized-KV decode. Upstream
  FlashAttention requires Ampere or newer and offers Turing only a separate
  third-party partial port; Volta is a generation below that. Every attention
  number in this repository depends on that component, and none of it is our
  work.

vLLM
